course: dictionary
lesson: 4916
title: Words that mean very big
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Immense means extremely large or great in size, amount or degree. It is a stronger word than big. A big hill is large, but an immense hill is enormous, far bigger than you expected.
explain: Read the words around immense to check its meaning. «Her head is free but her shoulders are nowhere to be found; she sees an immense length of neck rising like a stalk out of a sea of green leaves.» The neck rises above the leaves, which are really the tops of trees, so the neck must be very long. The clue «like a stalk» helps too.
explain: Immense can describe feelings as well as size. Immense joy or immense relief means a very strong feeling. Immense does not give a number, so use it when you want to show something is huge, not when you need an exact amount.
fact: Immense means extremely large or great in size, amount or degree.
fact: «An immense length of neck» means a very long neck.
fact: Immense is stronger than big: a big hill is large, but an immense hill is enormous.
fact: Immense does not give a number. It tells you something is huge without saying how huge.
fact: You can also use immense for feelings, such as immense joy or immense relief.
exercise: «She sees an immense length of neck.» What does immense mean here? | *Extremely large or great in size | Extremely long | Very quiet | Slightly warm
exercise: Which word is the strongest way to say something is big? | *immense | little | quiet | nice
exercise: Which sentence uses immense correctly? | I felt immense while I ate my lunch. | *The mountain was immense, far bigger than any hill near it. | The crumb was immense on the plate. | The pencil was immense for writing.
test: Mia felt immense relief when the bus finally arrived. What does immense mean here? | *Extremely great in feeling | Very small | Mildly tired | Extremely great
test: Why is immense not the same as a number? | It means the same as tiny. | It is only used for food. | It always gives an exact size. | *It shows something is huge without saying how huge.
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to immense? | quiet | tiny | *enormous | sleepy
